From f079b6f91f5a137a889b6197f86c73052520918a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 11:10:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] aux: gate the abandoned daemon's client close on the
 owner's shutdown sweep; document logging.debug_ssl_close

Follow-up to the two non-blocking nits in the exact-head review of #2074
(https://github.com/example-org/hermes/pull/2074#pullrequestreview-5889730795).

1. Close/shutdown race in aux_provider_handoff.release_client.
   The owner defers the close to each abandoned provider daemon, then
   shuts the client's sockets down (force_close_tcp_sockets). A daemon
   that finished between the defer and the sweep ran its close() while
   the owner was still in shutdown() on the same socket. sock_shutdown
   reads sock_fd outside the GIL, so it could shut down a recycled fd
   (ENOTSOCK on a file is harmless, but a recycled socket would be cut).
   The daemon-side release now waits on an Event that the owner sets
   right after its sweep (in a finally, so a sweep that raises still
   releases the daemons). The owner's own share of the countdown runs
   after the sweep as well.

2. logging.debug_ssl_close (read by hermes_logging.setup_logging for
   agent/ssl_close_tripwire.py) is now in DEFAULT_CONFIG's logging block
   (default false, same behaviour as an absent key), and
   website/docs/user-guide/configuration.md gains a Logging section that
   documents it together with level / max_size_mb / backup_count. Those
   three are dropped from the docs-drift baseline. config_defaults.py
   is at its FILE_LINES cap: max_size_mb and backup_count now share one
   line to offset the new key.

Proof:
- RED (handoff source reverted, new tests kept):
  test_daemon_finishing_during_the_owner_sweep_closes_only_after_it and
  test_a_failing_owner_sweep_still_releases_the_gated_daemon fail. The
  daemon's close lands between sweep-start and sweep-end.
- Mutant (try/finally around the sweep dropped): only
  test_a_failing_owner_sweep_still_releases_the_gated_daemon fails, because
  the daemon stays blocked.
- GREEN: test_aux_abandoned_provider_tls_fd.py 12/12, plus test_docs_drift
  and test_config (184 passed). The 40 test files that import
  aux_provider_handoff / ssl_close_tripwire / hermes_logging pass 422/422.
  check_docs_drift is ok, and scripts/check --base origin/main passes 19
  checks.

